\paragraph{Aspect 13: defining does not run the body.}
The critical aspect is that defining and invoking a function are two
separate acts --- the body runs only at a call.
The printed-greeting distractor encodes the \emph{function created but
not called} antipattern \autocite{Bosse2021Antipatterns}, which we
also observed in our own teaching.

