\paragraph{Aspect 15: return hands back a value, not a name.}
The critical aspect is that [[return]] hands back a \emph{value},
which the caller must capture in a name of its own; the local name
does not travel to the call site.
The value distractor encodes the observed misconception that
[[return]] \enquote{sends} the variable's name.

