\paragraph{Aspect 52: equal attributes do not make one object.}
The critical aspect is object identity: two objects may carry equal
attribute values and still be distinct, so an attribute is not an
object's identifier \autocite{Holland1997,Ragonis2005OOP}.
The same-object distractor encodes equal-attributes-same-object; the
error distractor encodes the catalogued belief that one attribute of
every object must be unique.
Form B probes the same aspect from the other side: two names bound to
\emph{one} object.

