\paragraph{Aspect 53: a method is defined once but acts per object.}
The critical aspect fuses the previous two: the method is defined in
the template, yet the call reaches only the object it is called on
--- the chapter's fusion example.
The all-objects distractor encodes the catalogued belief that the
class's methods have power over all its instances
\autocite{Ragonis2005OOP}.

